  <datafield tag="500" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">"This book is a contemporary, typographic exploration of The Story of O. The book is printed on a translucent paper with subsequent pages visible to the viewer. The shape of O in its various iterations: serif, sans-serif, regular, bold, script, upper and lowercase along with the color and feel of the paper further accentuate the sensuousness of the book."--Publisher's web site.</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="500" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">"Designed and digitally printed by Malini Gupta. The type used for the text was Meta Italic, by Erik Spiekermann." -- colophon.</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="500" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">Hand bound in Japanese stab binding, textblock enclosed between connected boards held together by a rubber band.</subfield>
  </datafield>
